general_comments.body:
@maciejmyslinski this PR has issues:
1) tests fail outside of node because of `global`
2) the place for the default check is wrong, and it doesn't handle missing locale specifications (like en-US ...)

Hey, sorry about adding my comments here, I'm not a contributor but I was browsing open PRs because I'm interested in improving a related area of functionality and I noticed some issues that could be addressed.

So feel free to ignore this -- I'm a nobody and it looks like this PR has a green light already.

But...

I'm not sure if introducing a magical constant `'default'` to `getSetGlobalLocale` is the right thing to do. What happens if someone tries to `moment.updateLocale('default', config)`? If it's going to be a magic constant, at the very least it shouldn't be a string (which _might_ potentially be mistaken for a valid locale). 

So define it as a proper constant, in the same way that the other constants in moment (eg. `moment.ISO_8601` and `moment.RFC_2822`) are defined...

    hooks.DEFAULT_LOCALE = function () {}

But now we've got this function just sitting there, couldn't we move the functionality from `getSetGlobalLocale` into there, to keep functions short and D.R.Y.
    
    hooks.DEFAULT_LOCALE = function () {
       let keys = /* environment sniffing logic goes here */;
       keys = keys || 'en';
       return keys;
    } 
    
    function getSetGlobalLocale(obj) {
       /* etc */
       if (obj === hooks.DEFAULT_LOCALE) {
          obj = obj();
       }
       /* etc. */
    }

But the implementation doesn't do this automatically, it only sniffs the locale if the constant was passed to `moment.locale`...

     // main.js
     import moment from 'moment';
     moment.locale(moment.DEFAULT_LOCALE)

and to make that a little less ugly, how about changing the `ALL_CAPS_CONSTANT` to a `lowerCamelCaseConstant` (and adding a `()` for the hell of it since it's only another two characters)...

    // main.js
    import moment from 'moment';
    // Tries to set the global locale from the browser's user string, otherwise defaults to `'en'`
    moment.locale(moment.defaultLocale());

    var mOtherLocale = moment().locale('my-other-locale'); 
    // I'd like my logs to be in my own language pls
    console.log(mOtherLocale.clone().locale(moment.defaultLocale()).format(DEBUG_DATE);

